<section id="doc-en">
  <h1>LG Extended - Complete Documentation</h1>

  <h2>1. Project Summary</h2>
  <p><strong>LG Extended</strong> is an Xposed module designed specifically for LG devices (mainly LG V60) that allows you to customize and modify various aspects of the system without having to modify the firmware. The module interacts with multiple system processes to apply changes in real time.</p>

  <p><strong>General Information:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- Name: LG Extended</li>
    <li>- Package: <code>com.zxerox.lg_extended</code></li>
    <li>- Version: 1.0 (versionCode: 1)</li>
    <li>- Author: ZxeroX</li>
    <li>- Min SDK: Android 10 (API 29)</li>
    <li>- Target SDK: Android 15 (API 35)</li>
    <li>- Framework: Xposed API 82+</li>
    <li>- Requirements: LSPosed or similar + Root (Magisk/KernelSU/APatch)</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Features:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- Battery icon customization with multiple styles (iOS 26, iOS 17, OneUI 8, OneUI 9)</li>
    <li>- Per-app DPI adjustment to change screen density individually</li>
    <li>- iOS-style recent apps that modifies the multitasking design</li>
    <li>- FLAG_SECURE bypass to allow screenshots in restricted apps</li>
    <li>- Settings icon customization with OneUI/HyperOS style icons</li>
    <li>- Custom profile card on the main Settings screen</li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>2. Architecture</h2>
  <p><code>MainHook.java</code> is the Xposed entry point that implements <code>IXposedHookLoadPackage</code>, <code>IXposedHookZygoteInit</code>, and <code>IXposedHookInitPackageResources</code>. It registers hooks based on the target package.</p>

  <h3>Hook Lifecycle</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>1. <strong>Initialization</strong>: <code>MainHook.initZygote()</code> stores the module path (<code>MODULE_PATH</code>)</li>
    <li>2. <strong>Load</strong>: <code>MainHook.handleLoadPackage()</code> detects the target package and registers hooks</li>
    <li>3. <strong>Registration</strong>: Each hook registers for its specific package (with try/catch in case it fails)</li>
    <li>4. <strong>Interception</strong>: Hooks modify behavior via <code>beforeHookedMethod</code> / <code>afterHookedMethod</code></li>
    <li>5. <strong>Persistence</strong>: Preferences are stored via <code>ModPrefs</code> ContentProvider</li>
    <li>6. <strong>Marking</strong>: MainHook marks each successful hook with <code>hook_active_{'{name}'}</code></li>
    <li>7. <strong>Logging</strong>: Each registered hook is logged with success/failure via <code>LogWriter</code></li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Packages Each Hook Intercepts</h3>
  <pre><code set:html={`handleLoadPackage(lpparam)
  │
  ├── "com.zxerox.lg_extended" → EXCLUDED (does not hook itself)
  │
  ├── ANY package:
  │       └── DpiHook (except the app itself)
  │
  ├── "com.android.systemui" or "com.lge.systemui":
  │       ├── QSPanelHook
  │       ├── ScrimHook
  │       ├── NotificationHook
  │       └── BatteryHook
  │
  ├── "com.lge.launcher3" or "com.android.launcher3":
  │       ├── RecentsHook
  │       └── LauncherHook
  │
  ├── "android":
  │       └── FlagSecureHook
  │
  └── "com.android.settings":
          └── SettingsHook`}></code></pre>

  <h3>Communication Pattern</h3>
  <p>The module uses a <strong>ContentProvider</strong> (<code>ModPrefs</code>) as a communication system between the configuration app (UI) and active hooks in different system processes.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>- UI Process → ContentResolver.insert() → ModPrefs (Module Process)</li>
    <li>- ModPrefs → ContentObserver.onChange() → Hooks (SystemUI, Launcher, etc.)</li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>3. How Hooks Work</h2>

  <h3>3.1 Fundamental Concepts</h3>
  <p>A <strong>hook</strong> is a technique that intercepts Android methods at runtime to modify their behavior without altering the original source code. LG Extended uses the <strong>Xposed</strong> framework for this.</p>

  <p><strong>Types of Hooks in Xposed:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>beforeHookedMethod</code>: Executes before the original method. Allows modifying parameters or canceling execution.</li>
    <li>- <code>afterHookedMethod</code>: Executes after the original method. Allows hiding views, injecting elements, or modifying the return.</li>
    <li>- <code>XC_MethodReplacement</code>: Completely replaces the method. Returns a fixed value or does nothing.</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong><code>hookSilently</code> Pattern:</strong></p>
  <p>RecursHook uses a helper pattern that wraps hooks in try/catch to avoid crashes if a class doesn't exist:</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`// If the class doesn't exist in this Android version, it's simply ignored
private void hookSilently(ClassLoader cl, String className, String method, Object... params) {
    try {
        XposedHelpers.findAndHookMethod(className, cl, method, params);
    } catch (Throwable t) {} // Silent - no crash
}`}></code></pre>

  <h3>3.2 ModPrefs - Communication System</h3>
  <p><strong>Authority:</strong> <code>com.zxerox.lg_extended.prefs</code></p>
  <p><strong>URI:</strong> <code>content://com.zxerox.lg_extended.prefs/prefs</code></p>
  <p>Hooks and the app communicate through a <strong>ContentProvider</strong>. The UI changes preferences and hooks read them in real time.</p>

  <p><strong>Write preferences (from UI):</strong></p>
  <pre><code set:html={`ContentValues values = new ContentValues();
values.put("key", "battery_style");
values.put("type", "string");
values.put("value", "IOS_26");
contentResolver.insert(ModPrefs.CONTENT_URI, values);
// ModPrefs notifies all registered ContentObservers`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Read preferences (from a hook):</strong></p>
  <pre><code set:html={`Cursor c = context.getContentResolver().query(
    ModPrefs.CONTENT_URI,
    new String[]{"battery_style"},  // key to read
    "string",                        // data type
    new String[]{"ONEUI_8"},         // default value
    null
);
if (c != null && c.moveToFirst()) {
    String value = c.getString(0);
    c.close();
}`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Real-time updates (ContentObserver):</strong></p>
  <p>BatteryHook registers an observer to apply style/color changes instantly without restarting SystemUI:</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`context.getContentResolver().registerContentObserver(
    Uri.parse("content://com.zxerox.lg_extended.prefs/prefs"),
    true, // Notify if any descendant changes
    new ContentObserver(new Handler(Looper.getMainLooper())) {
        @Override
        public void onChange(boolean selfChange) {
            // Re-read preferences and update ALL battery views
            BatteryIconView.Estilo newStyle = readSavedStyle(context);
            for (BatteryIconView v : batteries.values()) {
                v.setStyle(newStyle);
                applySavedColors(context, v);
            }
        }
    }
);`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Marking active hooks:</strong></p>
  <p>MainHook marks each successful hook in ModPrefs with the key <code>hook_active_{'{name}'}</code>. This allows the UI to show which hooks are running:</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`// In MainHook.markHookActive()
values.put("key", "hook_active_battery");
values.put("type", "boolean");
values.put("value", "true");
ctx.getContentResolver().insert(ModPrefs.CONTENT_URI, values);`}></code></pre>

  <h3>3.3 BatteryHook - Battery Icon Customization</h3>
  <p><strong>Target package:</strong> <code>com.android.systemui</code> / <code>com.lge.systemui</code></p>
  <p><strong>File:</strong> <code>hooks/BatteryHook.java</code></p>
  <p>Replaces the native LG battery icon (<code>LGBatteryMeterView</code>) with a custom <code>BatteryIconView</code> with multiple styles and colors.</p>

  <p><strong>Hook 1: <code>onAttachedToWindow</code></strong> - Executes when the battery view attaches to the view tree:</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`LGBatteryMeterView.onAttachedToWindow()
  → 1. Get reference to the original view
  → 2. Get the parent (ViewGroup)
  → 3. Hide the original view (setVisibility GONE)
  → 4. Create custom BatteryIconView
  → 5. Insert at SAME position as the original in the parent
  → 6. Register in WeakHashMap for tracking
  → 7. Apply saved colors from ModPrefs
  → 8. Register ContentObserver for real-time changes`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Hook 2: <code>onBatteryLevelChanged</code></strong> - Executes when battery level changes:</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`LGBatteryMeterView.onBatteryLevelChanged(level, plugged, charging)
  → 1. Hide original view (in case it becomes visible again)
  → 2. Hide percentage text (mBatteryLevel)
  → 3. Get BatteryIconView from WeakHashMap
  → 4. Call updateState(level, charging)`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Available styles:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>ONEUI_8</code>: Rounded pill style (default)</li>
    <li>- <code>ONEUI_9</code>: Loading circle style</li>
    <li>- <code>IOS_26</code>: iOS style with integrated bolt</li>
    <li>- <code>IOS_17</code>: iOS style with border and padding</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Default states and colors:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- Normal: background <code>#1C1C1E</code>, text white</li>
    <li>- Charging: background <code>#34C759</code>, text white</li>
    <li>- Low Battery (≤20%): background <code>#FF3B30</code>, text white</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Stored preferences:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>battery_style</code> (String): Selected style (ONEUI_8, ONEUI_9, IOS_26, IOS_17)</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_fondo</code> (int): Normal background color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_texto</code> (int): Normal text color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_borde</code> (int): Normal border color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_fondo_cargando</code> (int): Charging background color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_texto_cargando</code> (int): Charging text color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_borde_cargando</code> (int): Charging border color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_fondo_bajo</code> (int): Low battery background color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_texto_bajo</code> (int): Low battery text color</li>
    <li>- <code>battery_color_borde_bajo</code> (int): Low battery border color</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.4 DpiHook - DPI Change by Application</h3>
  <p><strong>Target package:</strong> All applications (except <code>com.zxerox.lg_extended</code>)</p>
  <p><strong>File:</strong> <code>hooks/DpiHook.java</code></p>
  <p>Modifies the screen density (DPI) of each application individually before Android renders the interface.</p>

  <p><strong>How it works step by step:</strong></p>
  <pre><code set:html={`ResourcesImpl.updateConfiguration(config, metrics, compatInfo)
  │
  ├── 1. First time executing? (dpiCache == -1)
  │       ├── YES: Read DPI saved in ModPrefs for this package
  │       │       └── Save to dpiCache (cached to avoid repeated queries)
  │       └── NO: Use already stored dpiCache
  │
  ├── 2. Is dpiCache <= 0? → Do nothing (use system DPI)
  │
  └── 3. Modify Configuration and DisplayMetrics
          ├── config.densityDpi = dpiCache
          ├── metrics.densityDpi = dpiCache
          └── metrics.density = dpiCache * 0.00625f`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Preferences:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>{'{package_name}'}</code> (int): Specific DPI for that app (0 = system default)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.5 RecentsHook - iOS Style for Multitasking</h3>
  <p><strong>Target package:</strong> <code>com.lge.launcher3</code> / <code>com.android.launcher3</code></p>
  <p><strong>File:</strong> <code>hooks/RecentsHook.java</code></p>
  <p>Modifies the recents view to implement an iOS-like style with stack effects, progressive scaling, and header transparency.</p>

  <p><strong>Intercepted methods (10+ using <code>hookSilently</code>):</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>TaskCornerRadius.get</code> (before): Rounds corners to 32dp</li>
    <li>- <code>TaskView.setFullscreenProgress</code> (after): Applies scale based on progress</li>
    <li>- <code>TaskView.setDimAlpha</code> (before): Removes dimming (fixed to 0)</li>
    <li>- <code>TaskThumbnailView.setDimAlpha</code> (before): Removes thumbnail dimming</li>
    <li>- <code>TaskThumbnailView.setDimAlphaMultipler</code> (before): Removes dimming multiplier</li>
    <li>- <code>TaskView.setStableAlpha</code> (before, ×2): Sets alpha to 1.0 (no transparency)</li>
    <li>- <code>RecentsView.setContentAlpha</code> (before): Controls content alpha</li>
    <li>- <code>TaskView.onFinishInflate</code> (after): Removes elevation (elevation = 0)</li>
    <li>- <code>TaskView.onTaskListVisibilityChanged</code> (before): Forces visible = true</li>
    <li>- <code>RecentsView.updateStackLayout</code> (before): Cancels original layout (DO_NOTHING)</li>
    <li>- <code>RecentsView.updateStackProperties</code> (after): <strong>Main hook</strong> - applies stack effect</li>
    <li>- <code>RecentsView.updateCurveProperties</code> (after, ×2): Reuses the same scrollHook</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Stack effect logic (scrollHook):</strong></p>
  <pre><code set:html={`RecentsView.updateStackProperties()
  → 1. Get scroll data (count, scrollX, width)
  → 2. Calculate native spacing (distance between first and second task view)
  → 3. For EACH task view:
      → Calculate distanceToCenter and progress (distance / spacing)
      → X TRANSLATION:
         - Left of center: progress * stackGapBehind
         - Right of center: progress * stackGapAhead
         - Center: translationX = 0
      → SCALE:
         - First 4 apps: 1.0 → 0.97
         - Rest: 0.97 (minimum 0.70)
         - Interpolated with fullscreenProgress
      → DEPTH: translationZ = child.getLeft() * 0.01
      → HEADER: scale 0.85, translateY 15f
      → Title alpha: max(0, 1 - |progress| * 2.5)
  → 4. Apply all transformations to the view`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Design parameters:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>STACK_GAP</code>: 150f (distance between apps in stack behind)</li>
    <li>- <code>stackGapAhead</code>: 65% of spacing (forward distance)</li>
    <li>- Initial scale: 1.0 - 0.97 (for first 4 apps)</li>
    <li>- Minimum scale: 0.70 (for distant apps)</li>
    <li>- Header scale: 0.85 (app title scale)</li>
    <li>- Header alpha threshold: 2.5 (title fade factor)</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Preferences:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>recents_enabled</code> (boolean): Enable iOS style in recents</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.6 FlagSecureHook - Restriction Bypass</h3>
  <p><strong>Target package:</strong> <code>android</code> (system process)</p>
  <p><strong>File:</strong> <code>hooks/FlagSecureHook.java</code></p>
  <p>Disables <code>FLAG_SECURE</code> which prevents screenshots in applications that implement it (banking apps, Netflix, etc.).</p>

  <p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>
  <pre><code set:html={`WindowState.isSecureLocked()
  → 1. Reload preferences from XML file (prefs.reload())
  → 2. Check if bypass is enabled
  │       └── prefs.getBoolean("bypass_flag_secure", true)
  → 3. If enabled:
          └── param.setResult(false) ← ALWAYS returns false
              (the original method NEVER executes)`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Important technical detail:</strong> This hook uses <code>XSharedPreferences</code> instead of <code>ModPrefs</code> because it runs in the <code>android</code> (system_server) process, where the app's ContentProvider is not available. It reads the preferences XML file directly.</p>

  <p><strong>Preferences:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>bypass_flag_secure</code> (boolean): Enable bypass (default: true)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.7 SettingsHook - Settings Customization</h3>
  <p><strong>Target package:</strong> <code>com.android.settings</code></p>
  <p><strong>File:</strong> <code>hooks/SettingsHook.java</code></p>
  <p>Performs extensive modifications to the Android Settings app.</p>

  <p><strong>Hook 1: Profile Card</strong> (<code>DashboardFragment.refreshAllPreferences</code>):</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`DashboardFragment.refreshAllPreferences()
  → 1. Check if it's TopLevelSettings (main screen)
  → 2. Read profile from ModPrefs (name, phrase, avatar)
  → 3. Build custom view (LinearLayout with avatar + text)
  → 4. Create LayoutPreference with the view
  → 5. Insert with order = -999 (always at top)
  → 6. Inject divider category with order = -998
  → 7. Modify AppBar (height 180dp, title 36sp)`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Hook 2: Icon Replacement</strong> (<code>PreferenceGroupAdapter.onBindViewHolder</code>):</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`PreferenceGroupAdapter.onBindViewHolder(holder, position)
  → 1. Get preference at that position
  → 2. Check if hook_settings_icons is enabled
  → 3. Get preference key
  → 4. Look up icon in iconMap (18 mappings)
  → 5. Load drawable from module resources
  │       └── XModuleResources.createInstance(MODULE_PATH)
  → 6. Replace holder's ImageView
  → 7. Remove tints and adjust size to 40dp`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Icon mappings (18):</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>top_level_network</code> → <code>ic_red_e_internet</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_connected_devices</code> → <code>ic_bluetooth</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_sound</code> → <code>ic_sonido</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_notification</code> → <code>ic_notificaciones</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_display</code> → <code>ic_pantalla</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_theme</code> → <code>ic_fondo_pantalla_y_tema</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_security</code> → <code>ic_pantalla_de_bloqueo_y_seguridad</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_privacy</code> → <code>ic_privacidad</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_location</code> → <code>ic_ubicacion</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_useful_features</code> → <code>ic_extensiones</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_apps_and_notifs</code> → <code>ic_aplicaciones</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_digital_wellbeing</code> → <code>ic_bienestar_digital</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_battery</code> → <code>ic_bateria</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_storage</code> → <code>ic_almacenamiento</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_emergency</code> → <code>ic_seguridad_y_emergencia</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_accounts</code> → <code>ic_cuentas</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_system</code> → <code>ic_sistema</code></li>
    <li>- <code>top_level_accessibility</code> → <code>ic_accesibilidad</code></li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Hook 3: Tint Lock</strong> (<code>DynamicIconColorDecorator</code>):</p>
  <pre><code set:html={`DynamicIconColorDecorator.setIconTint() / setDynamicIconColor()
  → 1. Get preference key
  → 2. Is it in the iconMap?
  │       └── YES: param.setResult(null) ← don't apply tint
  → 3. NO: leave original behavior`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Hook 4: Divider Removal:</strong></p>
  <pre><code set:html={`PreferenceFragmentCompat.setDivider()      → DO_NOTHING (no-op)
PreferenceFragmentCompat.setDividerHeight() → args[0] = 0
RecyclerView.addItemDecoration()            → block if contains "divider"
HIGHelper.isShowDivider()                   → returnConstant(false)`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Preferences:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>hook_settings_icons</code> (boolean): Replace settings icons</li>
    <li>- <code>profile_name</code> (String): Profile name</li>
    <li>- <code>profile_phrase</code> (String): Profile phrase</li>
    <li>- <code>profile_avatar_base64</code> (String): Avatar in Base64</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.8 LauncherHook - Automatic App Sorting</h3>
  <p><strong>Target package:</strong> <code>com.lge.launcher3</code> / <code>com.android.launcher3</code></p>
  <p><strong>File:</strong> <code>hooks/LauncherHook.java</code></p>
  <p>Automatically sorts apps alphabetically after a new app is installed.</p>

  <pre><code set:html={`AllAppsPagedView.addApps(apps, sessionId)
  → 1. Reload preferences
  → 2. Is hook_auto_sort_apps enabled?
  │       └── NO: Do nothing
  → 3. YES: Get enum SortType.NAME and call changeSortType(NAME)`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Preferences:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>- <code>hook_auto_sort_apps</code> (boolean): Automatically sort apps</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.9 QSPanelHook - MIUI Quick Settings Panel</h3>
  <p><strong>Target package:</strong> <code>com.android.systemui</code> / <code>com.lge.systemui</code></p>
  <p><strong>File:</strong> <code>hooks/QSPanelHook.java</code></p>
  <p>Makes the Quick Settings panel background transparent for a MIUI-style look.</p>

  <pre><code set:html={`QSContainerImpl.onFinishInflate()
  → 1. Check if pref_enable_miui_qs is enabled
  │     (also checks file /data/local/tmp/lg_ext_miui_qs)
  → 2. If enabled:
          ├── Find quick_settings_background view
          └── setBackgroundColor(Color.TRANSPARENT)`}></code></pre>

  <p><strong>Preferences:</strong></p>
